      <activity id="ad203297-b685-5bd6-b012-66651a91e90d" activityNameId="1bbe3876-de9d-5279-b18a-e3692c9fa9b4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production FR, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production FR, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 100% of the imported French natural gas to RoE was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 0 km is estimated for the pipeline export from France, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 0 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=a5f46fe1-47ca-3588-b743-d5c870fd6462
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of French natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a5f46fe1-47ca-3588-b743-d5c870fd6462.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
